From: lancethepants <lancethepants@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: allow vendor VHT on 2.4GHz in STA mode

0003 (vendor QAM-256 on 2.4GHz) predates the 6.9 conn-mode rework.
ieee80211_determine_ap_chan() now marks VHT unusable on 2.4GHz
unconditionally, so a client with HE disabled (or an HE-less AP)
dropped to HT even when both sides support vendor 256-QAM.

Only do that when the band lacks vendor_qam256_supported. The AP's VHT
operation on 2.4GHz uses the HT channel width, which
ieee80211_chandef_vht_oper() accepts as is.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -282,7 +282,8 @@
 			return IEEE80211_CONN_MODE_HT;
 		}
 		no_vht = true;
-	} else if (sband->band == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ) {
+	} else if (sband->band == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ &&
+		   !sband->vht_cap.vendor_qam256_supported) {
 		no_vht = true;
 	} else if (!ieee80211_chandef_vht_oper(&sdata->local->hw,
 					       vht_cap_info,
